'''Matthew Gordon Bullard''' (born June 5, 1967) is an American former professional [[basketball]] player in the [[National Basketball Association|NBA]] and former color analyst for the [[Houston Rockets]] on [[AT&T SportsNet Southwest]]. Bullard played 12 years professionally and 11 years in the NBA, most notably with the [[Houston Rockets]] from 1990 to 1994, and then again from 1996 to 2001. Other teams he played for include the [[Atlanta Hawks]], [[Charlotte Hornets]], and [[P.A.O.K. BC|PAOK]] in Greece.

