'''Mason Alexander Plumlee''' (born March 5, 1990), nicknamed "'''Plumdog Millionaire'''", is an American professional [[basketball]] player for the [[San Antonio Spurs]] of the [[National Basketball Association]] (NBA). He primarily plays the [[Center (basketball)|center]] position. As a freshman in 2009–10, he was a back-up forward for the [[Duke Blue Devils men's basketball|Duke Blue Devils]] [[2010 NCAA Men's Division I Basketball Tournament|national championship]] [[2009–10 Duke Blue Devils men's basketball team|team]], playing with his older brother [[Miles Plumlee|Miles]]. He was a 2009 [[McDonald's All-American Game|McDonald's All-American]] in high school.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.espn.com/college-sports/recruiting/basketball/mens/news/story?id=4496541|title=Plumlee finding way on the court|access-date=April 5, 2010|date=September 23, 2009|publisher=[[ESPN]]|author=Lawlor, Christopher|archive-date=July 21, 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130721155656/http://sports.espn.go.com/ncaa/recruiting/basketball/mens/news/story?id=4496541|url-status=live}}</ref> During his senior year at Duke, he also played with his younger brother [[Marshall Plumlee|Marshall]]. He was selected with the 22nd overall pick by the [[Brooklyn Nets]] in the [[2013 NBA draft]]. Plumlee was also a member of the [[United States men's national basketball team|United States national team]] that won a gold medal in the [[2014 United States FIBA Basketball World Cup team|2014 FIBA Basketball World Cup]].

